# American English: only the lines that differ from English. The rest is English.

disks-help-3 = You can see the drive the system runs from, but you can't make any change to it that erases or moves things. Every change to any drive asks for an administrator's password, each time. The eye hides a drive or partition from Folders and the ring. It stays here, grayed out, and it isn't locked.

disks-taken-back = The password you gave has now been canceled, so the next change will ask for one.
